# Seeding Script Rules

Seeding scripts populate Neo4j (or other stores) with baseline data. They must **never overwrite** existing data that users may have modified.

## Guard Before Seeding

Add a count guard at the start of the seed logic. Skip seeding entirely if the target nodes already exist:

```python
# GOOD: Guard and return early
result = session.run("MATCH (n:TargetLabel) RETURN count(n) AS cnt").single()
existing = result["cnt"] if result else 0
if existing > 0:
    logger.info("Skipped — %d TargetLabel(s) already present.", existing)
    return
# ... proceed with seeding
```

## Patterns to Avoid

- **MERGE ... SET** without a guard — overwrites all properties on every run
- **DETACH DELETE** then recreate — destroys user data
- Unconditional upserts that replace user-edited values

## Acceptable Patterns

- **Count guard** — skip if any target nodes exist
- **ON CREATE SET only** — create new nodes, never touch existing
- **Source-aware upsert** — only update when `source = 'seed'`; leave user-edited (`source <> 'seed'`) untouched
- **ON MATCH SET** limited to non-user fields (e.g. `patient_count`, `meta`) — preserve user-defined filters/config

## Docstring

Document the guard in the module docstring:

```python
"""Seed X into the Knowledge Graph.

Only seeds when no X nodes exist; skips if any are already present
to avoid overwriting user-modified data.
"""
```
